5
00:01:17,533 --> 00:01:18,532
Smeagol!

6
00:01:19,459 --> 00:01:21,701
I've got one!

7
00:01:22,337 --> 00:01:24,330
I've got a fish, Smea... Smeagol!

8
00:01:24,506 --> 00:01:27,623
Pull it in. Go on. Go on. Go on. Pull it in.

9
00:01:35,847 --> 00:01:37,674
Deagol!

10
00:02:35,060 --> 00:02:36,886
Deagol?

11
00:02:39,439 --> 00:02:41,679
Deagol.

12
00:02:57,494 --> 00:02:59,570
Give us that, Deagol, my love.

13
00:03:04,541 --> 00:03:05,822
Why?

14
00:03:06,918 --> 00:03:09,159
Because...

15
00:03:09,335 --> 00:03:13,084
it's my birthday and I wants it.

16
00:04:47,121 --> 00:04:52,363
My precious.

17
00:04:59,922 --> 00:05:02,839
They cursed us.

18
00:05:03,008 --> 00:05:04,383
Murderer.

19
00:05:04,552 --> 00:05:07,006
"Murderer" they called us.

20
00:05:07,178 --> 00:05:11,968
They cursed us and drove us away.

21
00:05:13,099 --> 00:05:14,806
Gollum.

22
00:05:14,974 --> 00:05:16,683
Gollum.

23
00:05:16,852 --> 00:05:18,808
Gollum.

24
00:05:22,356 --> 00:05:25,356
And we wept, precious.

25
00:05:25,524 --> 00:05:29,107
We wept to be so alone.

26
00:05:31,696 --> 00:05:35,480
- and cool
- So nice for feet

27
00:05:36,493 --> 00:05:40,868
And we only wish To catch a fish

28
00:05:41,037 --> 00:05:44,287
So juicy sweet

29
00:05:50,045 --> 00:05:54,170
And we forgot the taste of bread...

30
00:05:54,338 --> 00:05:57,956
the sound of trees...

31
00:05:58,842 --> 00:06:02,045
the softness of the wind.

32
00:06:02,678 --> 00:06:08,348
We even forgot our own name.

33
00:06:16,482 --> 00:06:22,897
My precious.

34
00:07:07,145 --> 00:07:09,386
Wake up!

35
00:07:10,440 --> 00:07:12,099
Wake up!

36
00:07:12,274 --> 00:07:14,066
Wake up, sleepies.

37
00:07:14,234 --> 00:07:16,107
We must go, yes.

38
00:07:16,278 --> 00:07:18,947
We must go at once.

39
00:07:22,490 --> 00:07:25,574
Haven't you had any sleep, Mr. Frodo?

40
00:07:27,786 --> 00:07:30,324
I've gone and had too much.

41
00:07:31,706 --> 00:07:33,449
Must be getting late.

42
00:07:33,624 --> 00:07:35,119
No.

43
00:07:35,293 --> 00:07:37,200
It isn't.

44
00:07:37,376 --> 00:07:40,412
It isn't midday yet.

45
00:07:40,588 --> 00:07:43,161
The days are growing darker.

46
00:07:47,427 --> 00:07:49,634
Come on!

47
00:07:52,055 --> 00:07:54,296
Must go! No time!

48
00:07:54,473 --> 00:07:56,845
Not before Mr. Frodo's had something to eat.

49
00:07:57,017 --> 00:07:59,887
No time to lose, silly.

50
00:08:08,651 --> 00:08:09,931
Here.

51
00:08:13,156 --> 00:08:14,981
What about you?

52
00:08:15,156 --> 00:08:18,525
Oh, no, I'm not hungry.
Leastways, not for lembas bread.

53
00:08:19,119 --> 00:08:20,493
Sam.

54
00:08:23,079 --> 00:08:24,621
All right.

55
00:08:24,788 --> 00:08:27,279
We don't have that much left.

56
00:08:27,458 --> 00:08:30,328
We have to be careful or we're going to run out.

57
00:08:32,503 --> 00:08:35,420
You go ahead and eat that, Mr. Frodo.

58
00:08:35,588 --> 00:08:36,999
I've rationed it.

59
00:08:37,507 --> 00:08:39,166
There should be enough.

60
00:08:41,343 --> 00:08:42,541
For what?

61
00:08:44,221 --> 00:08:45,964
The journey home.

62
00:08:53,811 --> 00:08:56,135
Come, Hobbitses.

63
00:08:57,522 --> 00:08:59,396
Very close now.

64
00:08:59,566 --> 00:09:02,815
Very close to Mordor.

65
00:09:02,985 --> 00:09:05,653
No safe places here.

66
00:09:05,820 --> 00:09:07,978
Hurry.

67
00:10:00,363 --> 00:10:02,071
It's good.

68
00:10:02,991 --> 00:10:04,733
Definitely from the Shire.

69
00:10:06,951 --> 00:10:09,074
Longbottom Leaf.

70
00:10:14,416 --> 00:10:18,745
I feel like I'm back at The Green Dragon.

71
00:10:19,836 --> 00:10:23,085
- Green Dragon.
- A mug of ale in my hand.

72
00:10:23,255 --> 00:10:27,834
Putting my feet up on a settle after a hard day's work.

73
00:10:28,427 --> 00:10:31,877
Only, you've never done a hard day's work.

74
00:10:44,689 --> 00:10:47,725
Welcome, my lords...

75
00:10:47,900 --> 00:10:50,141
to Isengard!

76
00:10:50,527 --> 00:10:54,274
You young rascals! A merry hunt you've led us on...

77
00:10:54,446 --> 00:10:59,440
and now we find you feasting and... and smoking!

78
00:10:59,618 --> 00:11:02,784
We are sitting on a field of victory...

79
00:11:02,953 --> 00:11:06,452
enjoying a few well-earned comforts.

80
00:11:07,540 --> 00:11:11,371
The salted pork is particularly good.

81
00:11:11,919 --> 00:11:14,291
Salted pork?

82
00:11:15,505 --> 00:11:18,919
- Hobbits.
- We're under orders from Treebeard...

83
00:11:19,090 --> 00:11:21,925
who's taken over management of Isengard.

84
00:11:24,469 --> 00:11:27,470
Young Master Gandalf.

85
00:11:27,639 --> 00:11:32,217
I'm glad you've come.

86
00:11:32,393 --> 00:11:36,804
Wood and water, stock and stone I can master.

87
00:11:36,979 --> 00:11:40,644
But there is a wizard to manage here...

88
00:11:40,815 --> 00:11:42,808
locked in his tower.

89
00:11:45,486 --> 00:11:46,815
Show yourself.

90
00:11:47,071 --> 00:11:48,777
Be careful.

91
00:11:49,571 --> 00:11:52,241
Even in defeat, Saruman is dangerous.

92
00:11:52,408 --> 00:11:54,531
Well, let's just have his head and be done with it.

93
00:11:54,702 --> 00:11:56,740
No.

94
00:11:57,078 --> 00:11:59,403
We need him alive.

95
00:12:00,415 --> 00:12:02,987
We need him to talk.

96
00:12:04,876 --> 00:12:09,086
You have fought many wars and
slain many men, Theoden King...

97
00:12:09,254 --> 00:12:10,748
and made peace afterwards.

98
00:12:10,922 --> 00:12:15,880
Can we not take counsel together
as we once did, my old friend?

99
00:12:16,051 --> 00:12:19,253
Can we not have peace, you and I?

100
00:12:19,428 --> 00:12:21,337
We shall have peace.

101
00:12:23,265 --> 00:12:25,388
We shall have peace...

102
00:12:25,559 --> 00:12:29,602
when you answer for the burning of the Westfold...

103
00:12:29,771 --> 00:12:32,521
and the children that lie dead there!

104
00:12:33,273 --> 00:12:37,436
We shall have peace when the lives of the soldiers...

105
00:12:37,609 --> 00:12:39,686
whose bodies were hewn even as they lay dead...

106
00:12:39,862 --> 00:12:43,396
against the gates of the Hornburg, are avenged!

107
00:12:44,949 --> 00:12:50,534
When you hang from a gibbet for
the sport of your own crows...

108
00:12:51,453 --> 00:12:53,695
we shall have peace.

109
00:12:56,458 --> 00:12:59,161
Gibbets and crows?

110
00:12:59,502 --> 00:13:00,746
Dotard!

111
00:13:02,211 --> 00:13:05,046
What do you want, Gandalf Greyhame?

112
00:13:06,047 --> 00:13:08,539
Let me guess. The Key of Orthanc.

113
00:13:08,717 --> 00:13:11,634
Or perhaps the Keys of Barad-dur itself...

114
00:13:11,803 --> 00:13:15,799
along with the crowns of the seven
kings and the rods of the Five Wizards!

115
00:13:15,973 --> 00:13:18,925
Your treachery has already cost many lives.

116
00:13:19,100 --> 00:13:21,472
Thousands more are now at risk.

117
00:13:21,644 --> 00:13:24,015
But you could save them, Saruman.

118
00:13:24,187 --> 00:13:26,475
You were deep in the enemy's counsel.

119
00:13:26,648 --> 00:13:29,932
So you have come here for information.

120
00:13:30,817 --> 00:13:32,644
I have some for you.

121
00:13:38,114 --> 00:13:41,068
Something festers in the heart of Middle-earth.

122
00:13:41,242 --> 00:13:43,484
Something that you have failed to see.

123
00:13:45,996 --> 00:13:49,494
But the Great Eye has seen it.

124
00:13:50,541 --> 00:13:54,240
Even now he presses his advantage.

125
00:13:56,003 --> 00:13:59,337
His attack will come soon.

126
00:14:01,549 --> 00:14:03,672
You're all going to die.

127
00:14:06,178 --> 00:14:09,427
But you know this, don't you, Gandalf?

128
00:14:09,597 --> 00:14:14,223
You cannot think that this Ranger will
ever sit upon the throne of Gondor.

129
00:14:14,394 --> 00:14:20,477
This exile, crept from the
shadows, will never be crowned king.

130
00:14:21,816 --> 00:14:25,479
Gandalf does not hesitate to
sacrifice those closest to him...

131
00:14:26,402 --> 00:14:28,608
those he professes to love.

132
00:14:29,655 --> 00:14:34,196
Tell me, what words of comfort
did you give the Halfling...

133
00:14:34,366 --> 00:14:37,402
before you sent him to his doom?

134
00:14:39,829 --> 00:14:44,538
The path that you have set
him on can only lead to death.

135
00:14:44,875 --> 00:14:47,033
I've heard enough!

136
00:14:47,210 --> 00:14:49,035
Shoot him. Stick an arrow in his gob.

137
00:14:49,544 --> 00:14:51,204
No.

138
00:14:51,672 --> 00:14:53,878
Come down, Saruman...

139
00:14:54,049 --> 00:14:57,997
- and your life will be spared.
- Save your pity and your mercy.

140
00:14:58,177 --> 00:14:59,505
I have no use for it!

141
00:15:08,726 --> 00:15:10,185
Saruman...

142
00:15:11,229 --> 00:15:14,395
your staff is broken.

143
00:15:25,281 --> 00:15:28,732
Grima, you need not follow him.

144
00:15:29,909 --> 00:15:32,578
You were not always as you are now.

145
00:15:32,745 --> 00:15:35,579
You were once a Man of Rohan.

146
00:15:35,747 --> 00:15:36,992
Come down.

147
00:15:37,165 --> 00:15:39,870
A Man of Rohan?

148
00:15:40,794 --> 00:15:43,035
What is the house of Rohan...

149
00:15:43,212 --> 00:15:46,876
but a thatched barn where brigands drink in the reek...

150
00:15:47,047 --> 00:15:50,748
and their brats roll on the floor with the dogs?

151
00:15:51,260 --> 00:15:57,712
The victory at Helm's Deep does not
belong to you, Theoden Horse-master.

152
00:15:58,349 --> 00:16:02,925
You are a lesser son of greater sires.

153
00:16:05,270 --> 00:16:06,978
Grima...

154
00:16:07,814 --> 00:16:09,687
come down.

155
00:16:10,024 --> 00:16:11,435
Be free of him.

156
00:16:11,610 --> 00:16:15,605
- Free? He will never be free.
- No.

157
00:16:15,986 --> 00:16:18,608
Get down, cur!

158
00:16:20,365 --> 00:16:21,646
Saruman!

159
00:16:21,825 --> 00:16:24,445
You were deep in the enemy's counsel.

160
00:16:24,952 --> 00:16:27,111
Tell us what you know!

161
00:16:28,623 --> 00:16:33,863
You withdraw your guard, and I will
tell you where your doom will be decided.

162
00:16:34,042 --> 00:16:37,577
I will not be held prisoner here.

163
00:17:04,691 --> 00:17:06,234
Send word to all our allies...

164
00:17:06,401 --> 00:17:09,319
and to every corner of
Middle-earth that still stands free.

165
00:17:09,862 --> 00:17:12,982
The enemy moves against us. We
need to know where he will strike.

166
00:17:32,171 --> 00:17:36,120
The filth of Saruman...

167
00:17:36,299 --> 00:17:40,130
is washing away.

168
00:17:40,303 --> 00:17:44,844
Trees will come back to live here.

169
00:17:45,347 --> 00:17:47,506
Young trees.

170
00:17:47,683 --> 00:17:49,888
- Wild trees.
- Pippin!

171
00:17:59,358 --> 00:18:01,517
Bless my bark!

172
00:18:01,694 --> 00:18:03,567
Peregrin Took!

173
00:18:03,738 --> 00:18:06,358
I'll take that, my lad.

174
00:18:06,530 --> 00:18:08,405
Quickly, now.

175
00:18:58,571 --> 00:19:04,156
Tonight we remember those who gave
their blood to defend this country.

176
00:19:04,826 --> 00:19:06,866
Hail the victorious dead.

177
00:19:07,036 --> 00:19:08,446
Hail!

178
00:19:19,421 --> 00:19:21,330
No pauses.

179
00:19:21,506 --> 00:19:25,669
- No spills.
- And no regurgitation.

180
00:19:26,176 --> 00:19:27,835
So it's a drinking game?

181
00:19:29,387 --> 00:19:32,090
Last one standing wins.

182
00:19:36,434 --> 00:19:38,427
What'll we drink to? Let's drink to victory!

183
00:19:38,603 --> 00:19:40,013
To victory!

184
00:19:52,197 --> 00:19:54,347
[Rohirric] <i>Westu Aragorn hál.</i>
[English] Be-thou Aragorn well!

185
00:20:23,971 --> 00:20:25,631
I am happy for you.

186
00:20:26,014 --> 00:20:28,421
He is an honorable man.

187
00:20:28,849 --> 00:20:31,304
You are both honorable men.

188
00:20:33,145 --> 00:20:38,482
It was not Theoden of Rohan
who led our people to victory.

189
00:20:46,655 --> 00:20:48,481
Don't listen to me.

190
00:20:49,324 --> 00:20:50,817
You are young.

191
00:20:50,991 --> 00:20:53,317
And tonight is for you.

192
00:21:07,671 --> 00:21:09,331
Here, here.

193
00:21:10,841 --> 00:21:16,758
It's the Dwarves that go
swimming with little, hairy women.

194
00:21:22,141 --> 00:21:23,385
I feel something.

195
00:21:25,519 --> 00:21:28,008
A slight tingle in my fingers.

196
00:21:28,729 --> 00:21:30,305
I think it's affecting me.

197
00:21:32,232 --> 00:21:33,939
What did I say?

198
00:21:34,108 --> 00:21:37,442
He can't hold his liquor.

199
00:21:44,783 --> 00:21:46,111
Game over.

200
00:21:46,283 --> 00:21:49,700
Oh, you can search far and wide
You can drink the whole town dry

201
00:21:49,870 --> 00:21:53,819
But you'll never find a beer so brown
But you'll never find a beer so brown

202
00:21:53,999 --> 00:21:58,374
As the one we drink in our hometown
As the one we drink in our hometown

203
00:21:58,544 --> 00:22:02,457
You can drink your fancy ales
You can drink them by the flagon

204
00:22:02,630 --> 00:22:05,796
But the only brew for the brave and true

205
00:22:08,428 --> 00:22:09,706
Pippin!

206
00:22:10,178 --> 00:22:13,213
But the only brew for the brave and true

207
00:22:13,555 --> 00:22:16,260
Comes from The Green Dragon

208
00:22:18,977 --> 00:22:21,811
Thank you! I win!

209
00:22:23,564 --> 00:22:26,053
No news of Frodo?

210
00:22:26,231 --> 00:22:29,731
No word. Nothing.

211
00:22:30,569 --> 00:22:32,727
We have time.

212
00:22:34,238 --> 00:22:37,523
Every day, Frodo moves closer to Mordor.

213
00:22:38,283 --> 00:22:40,359
Do we know that?

214
00:22:44,204 --> 00:22:45,912
What does your heart tell you?

215
00:22:52,962 --> 00:22:56,294
That Frodo is alive.

216
00:22:58,465 --> 00:23:00,256
Yes.

217
00:23:02,844 --> 00:23:05,001
Yes, he's alive.

218
00:23:07,264 --> 00:23:10,098
Too risky. Too risky.

219
00:23:10,266 --> 00:23:11,511
Thieves.

220
00:23:11,684 --> 00:23:13,722
They stole it from us.

221
00:23:13,893 --> 00:23:17,393
Kill them. Kill them. Kill them both.

222
00:23:19,440 --> 00:23:22,274
Quiet! Mustn't wake them.

223
00:23:22,442 --> 00:23:24,979
Mustn't ruin it now.

224
00:23:25,152 --> 00:23:27,229
But they knows.

225
00:23:27,405 --> 00:23:29,277
They knows.

226
00:23:29,447 --> 00:23:32,068
They suspects us.

227
00:23:33,284 --> 00:23:36,817
What's it saying, my precious, my love?

228
00:23:36,995 --> 00:23:40,576
Is Smeagol losing his nerve?

229
00:23:41,248 --> 00:23:43,619
No. Not.

230
00:23:43,792 --> 00:23:48,038
Never. Smeagol hates nasty Hobbitses.

231
00:23:48,212 --> 00:23:53,039
Smeagol wants to see them dead.

232
00:23:53,216 --> 00:23:55,753
And we will.

233
00:23:55,926 --> 00:23:59,970
Smeagol did it once. He can do it again.

234
00:24:03,307 --> 00:24:05,977
It's ours!

235
00:24:06,143 --> 00:24:08,812
Ours!

236
00:24:09,937 --> 00:24:12,807
We must get the precious. We must get it back.

237
00:24:12,981 --> 00:24:16,396
Patience! Patience, my love.

238
00:24:16,567 --> 00:24:20,945
First we must lead them to her.

239
00:24:21,822 --> 00:24:26,814
We lead them to the Winding Stair.

240
00:24:26,992 --> 00:24:29,661
Yes, the stairs. And then?

241
00:24:29,828 --> 00:24:32,827
Up, up, up, up, up the stairs we go...

242
00:24:32,997 --> 00:24:39,412
until we come to the tunnel.

243
00:24:39,793 --> 00:24:42,913
And when they go in...

244
00:24:43,088 --> 00:24:45,875
there's no coming out.

245
00:24:46,799 --> 00:24:49,670
She's always hungry.

246
00:24:50,428 --> 00:24:54,636
She always needs to feed.

247
00:24:54,804 --> 00:24:56,215
She must eat.

248
00:24:56,390 --> 00:24:58,512
All she gets is filthy Orcses.

249
00:24:58,684 --> 00:25:01,435
And they doesn't taste very nice, does they, precious?

250
00:25:02,062 --> 00:25:03,685
No.

251
00:25:03,854 --> 00:25:08,562
Not very nice at all, my love.

252
00:25:08,733 --> 00:25:11,519
She hungers for sweeter meats.

253
00:25:11,693 --> 00:25:13,520
Hobbit meat.

254
00:25:13,694 --> 00:25:18,522
And when she throws away the
bones and the empty clothes...

255
00:25:18,699 --> 00:25:21,783
then we will find it.

256
00:25:21,952 --> 00:25:26,278
And take it for me!

257
00:25:28,039 --> 00:25:29,450
For us.

258
00:25:29,958 --> 00:25:32,959
Yes. We meant "for us."

259
00:25:33,127 --> 00:25:36,578
Gollum. Gollum.

260
00:25:36,755 --> 00:25:41,250
The precious will be ours...

261
00:25:41,424 --> 00:25:45,920
once the Hobbitses are dead!

262
00:25:46,429 --> 00:25:47,888
You treacherous little toad!

263
00:25:50,598 --> 00:25:52,886
No! No! Master!

264
00:25:53,058 --> 00:25:54,683
No, Sam! Leave him alone!

265
00:25:55,561 --> 00:25:58,229
I heard it from his own mouth. He means to murder us.

266
00:25:58,395 --> 00:26:02,559
Never! Smeagol wouldn't hurt a fly.

267
00:26:04,068 --> 00:26:06,640
He's a horrid, fat Hobbit...

268
00:26:06,820 --> 00:26:08,397
who hates Smeagol...

269
00:26:08,570 --> 00:26:11,358
and who makes up nasty lies.

270
00:26:11,532 --> 00:26:14,199
You miserable little maggot! I'll stove your head in!

271
00:26:14,575 --> 00:26:15,855
Sam!

272
00:26:16,243 --> 00:26:18,532
Call me a liar? You're a liar!

273
00:26:19,496 --> 00:26:23,408
- You scare him off, we're lost!
- I don't care! I can't do it, Mr. Frodo.

274
00:26:23,582 --> 00:26:26,749
- I won't wait around for him to kill us!
- I'm not sending him away.

275
00:26:27,085 --> 00:26:28,414
You don't see it, do you?

276
00:26:28,837 --> 00:26:30,246
He's a villain.

277
00:26:31,255 --> 00:26:34,873
We can't do this by ourselves,
Sam. Not without a guide.

278
00:26:35,718 --> 00:26:38,586
I need you on my side.

279
00:26:39,386 --> 00:26:41,711
I'm on your side, Mr. Frodo.

280
00:26:43,223 --> 00:26:46,176
I know, Sam. I know.

281
00:26:46,725 --> 00:26:48,718
Trust me.

282
00:26:48,894 --> 00:26:51,266
Come, Smeagol.

283
00:27:59,198 --> 00:28:00,657
What time is it?

284
00:28:02,994 --> 00:28:04,487
Not yet dawn.

285
00:28:11,415 --> 00:28:14,451
I dreamed I saw a great wave...

286
00:28:14,626 --> 00:28:18,625
climbing over green lands and above the hills.

287
00:28:19,881 --> 00:28:22,335
I stood upon the brink.

288
00:28:23,258 --> 00:28:26,425
It was utterly dark in the abyss before my feet.

289
00:28:28,345 --> 00:28:31,132
A light shone behind me...

290
00:28:31,765 --> 00:28:34,173
but I could not turn.

291
00:28:34,351 --> 00:28:37,765
I could only stand there, waiting.

292
00:28:39,229 --> 00:28:41,933
Night changes many thoughts.

293
00:28:42,315 --> 00:28:44,473
Sleep, Eowyn.

294
00:28:45,025 --> 00:28:47,267
Sleep...

295
00:28:49,988 --> 00:28:51,860
while you can.

296
00:29:16,007 --> 00:29:18,296
The stars are veiled.

297
00:29:19,303 --> 00:29:22,799
Something stirs in the east.

298
00:29:23,471 --> 00:29:26,590
A sleepless malice.

299
00:29:28,601 --> 00:29:31,387
The Eye of the enemy is moving.

300
00:29:44,822 --> 00:29:47,526
What are you doing?

301
00:29:52,160 --> 00:29:53,618
Pippin!

302
00:30:01,127 --> 00:30:02,869
Pippin?

303
00:30:15,762 --> 00:30:17,091
Pippin.

304
00:30:17,764 --> 00:30:20,432
- What, are you mad?
- I just want to look at it.

305
00:30:20,599 --> 00:30:21,713
Just one more time.

306
00:30:21,975 --> 00:30:24,051
Put it back.

307
00:30:34,319 --> 00:30:36,109
Pippin.

308
00:30:42,616 --> 00:30:44,111
No!

309
00:30:49,204 --> 00:30:50,449
Pippin.

310
00:30:53,792 --> 00:30:54,990
He is here.

311
00:30:55,168 --> 00:30:57,455
I see you.

312
00:31:00,463 --> 00:31:02,088
Pippin!

313
00:31:16,727 --> 00:31:19,477
Help! Gandalf, help!

314
00:31:21,229 --> 00:31:23,102
Someone help him!

315
00:31:29,486 --> 00:31:30,684
Pippin!

316
00:31:31,822 --> 00:31:33,066
Fool of a Took!

317
00:31:54,171 --> 00:31:56,378
Look at me.

318
00:31:58,342 --> 00:32:02,469
Gandalf, forgive me.

319
00:32:02,637 --> 00:32:04,510
Look at me.

320
00:32:04,679 --> 00:32:06,507
What did you see?

321
00:32:10,017 --> 00:32:12,093
A tree.

322
00:32:13,062 --> 00:32:14,936
There was a white tree...

323
00:32:15,106 --> 00:32:16,599
in a courtyard of stone.

324
00:32:19,400 --> 00:32:20,679
It was dead.

325
00:32:24,862 --> 00:32:26,688
The city was burning.

326
00:32:26,863 --> 00:32:30,233
Minas Tirith? Is that what you saw?

327
00:32:30,910 --> 00:32:32,947
I saw...

328
00:32:36,329 --> 00:32:37,705
I saw him.

329
00:32:40,708 --> 00:32:42,950
I could hear his voice in my head.

330
00:32:43,127 --> 00:32:45,534
And what did you tell him?

331
00:32:45,712 --> 00:32:47,538
Speak!

332
00:32:51,716 --> 00:32:54,881
He asked me my name. I didn't answer.

333
00:32:55,052 --> 00:32:56,511
He hurt me.

334
00:32:56,679 --> 00:32:59,134
What did you tell him about Frodo and the Ring?

335
00:33:02,642 --> 00:33:05,096
There was no lie in Pippin's eyes.

336
00:33:05,935 --> 00:33:08,177
A fool...

337
00:33:08,354 --> 00:33:10,642
but an honest fool he remains.

338
00:33:11,106 --> 00:33:14,641
He told Sauron nothing of Frodo and the Ring.

339
00:33:15,694 --> 00:33:18,065
We've been strangely fortunate.

340
00:33:18,237 --> 00:33:22,103
Pippin saw in the palantir a
glimpse of the enemy's plan.

341
00:33:23,033 --> 00:33:26,981
Sauron moves to strike the city of Minas Tirith.

342
00:33:27,578 --> 00:33:31,326
His defeat at Helm's Deep showed our enemy one thing.

343
00:33:31,498 --> 00:33:33,822
He knows the heir of Elendil has come forth.

344
00:33:33,998 --> 00:33:36,121
Men are not as weak as he supposed.

345
00:33:36,292 --> 00:33:40,076
There is courage still, strength
enough perhaps to challenge him.

346
00:33:40,296 --> 00:33:42,169
Sauron fears this.

347
00:33:42,338 --> 00:33:46,668
He will not risk the peoples of
Middle-earth uniting under one banner.

348
00:33:47,843 --> 00:33:50,250
He will raze Minas Tirith to the ground...

349
00:33:50,428 --> 00:33:53,927
before he sees a king return to the throne of Men.

350
00:33:54,098 --> 00:33:58,011
If the beacons of Gondor are
lit, Rohan must be ready for war.

351
00:33:58,935 --> 00:34:01,141
Tell me...

352
00:34:01,312 --> 00:34:05,095
why should we ride to the aid of
those who did not come to ours?

353
00:34:08,984 --> 00:34:10,811
What do we owe Gondor?

354
00:34:11,945 --> 00:34:13,984
- I will go.
- No!

355
00:34:14,155 --> 00:34:17,320
- They must be warned.
- They will be.

356
00:34:20,744 --> 00:34:23,281
You must come to Minas Tirith by another road.

357
00:34:23,829 --> 00:34:28,290
Follow the river. Look to the black ships.

358
00:34:29,250 --> 00:34:31,208
Understand this:

359
00:34:31,377 --> 00:34:35,041
Things are now in motion that cannot be undone.

360
00:34:36,548 --> 00:34:38,622
I ride for Minas Tirith...

361
00:34:40,884 --> 00:34:43,554
and I won't be going alone.

362
00:34:45,304 --> 00:34:48,968
Of all the inquisitive Hobbits,
Peregrin Took, you are the worst.

363
00:34:49,974 --> 00:34:51,635
Hurry! Hurry!

364
00:34:53,144 --> 00:34:54,553
Where are we going?

365
00:34:54,728 --> 00:34:55,973
Why did you look?

366
00:34:56,147 --> 00:34:58,897
Why do you always have to look?

367
00:34:59,065 --> 00:35:02,147
- I don't know. I can't help it.
- You never can.

368
00:35:02,609 --> 00:35:04,019
I'm sorry, all right?

369
00:35:06,112 --> 00:35:09,029
- I won't do it again.
- Don't you understand?

370
00:35:09,782 --> 00:35:11,738
The enemy thinks you have the Ring.

371
00:35:11,908 --> 00:35:15,656
He's going to be looking for you,
Pip. They have to get you out of here.

372
00:35:17,078 --> 00:35:19,748
And you...? You're coming with me?

373
00:35:21,958 --> 00:35:23,368
Merry?

374
00:35:23,543 --> 00:35:24,822
Come on.

375
00:35:30,340 --> 00:35:31,715
How far is Minas Tirith?

376
00:35:31,882 --> 00:35:34,502
Three days' ride, as the Nazgul flies.

377
00:35:34,675 --> 00:35:38,175
And you better hope we don't
have one of those on our tail.

378
00:35:38,888 --> 00:35:40,381
Here.

379
00:35:40,555 --> 00:35:42,347
Something for the road.

380
00:35:43,225 --> 00:35:45,181
The last of the Longbottom Leaf.

381
00:35:45,352 --> 00:35:49,347
I know you've run out. You smoke too much, Pippin.

382
00:35:49,520 --> 00:35:52,011
But... But we'll see each other soon.

383
00:35:55,359 --> 00:35:57,849
- Won't we?
- I don't know.

384
00:35:59,863 --> 00:36:01,901
I don't know what's going to happen.

385
00:36:02,072 --> 00:36:03,779
- Merry.
- Run, Shadowfax.

386
00:36:03,948 --> 00:36:05,406
Show us the meaning of haste.

387
00:36:05,574 --> 00:36:07,484
Merry!

388
00:36:17,960 --> 00:36:19,074
Merry!

389
00:36:29,552 --> 00:36:31,045
He's always followed me...

390
00:36:31,720 --> 00:36:33,759
everywhere I went...

391
00:36:34,097 --> 00:36:35,887
since before we were tweens.

392
00:36:37,057 --> 00:36:40,971
I would get him into the worst sort of trouble...

393
00:36:41,144 --> 00:36:43,219
but I was always there to get him out.

394
00:36:45,688 --> 00:36:47,563
Now he's gone.

395
00:36:49,234 --> 00:36:52,150
Just like Frodo and Sam.

396
00:36:52,778 --> 00:36:55,529
One thing I have learned about Hobbits:

397
00:36:55,697 --> 00:36:57,358
They're a most hardy folk.

398
00:36:57,907 --> 00:37:01,606
Foolhardy, maybe. He's a Took.

399
00:37:16,087 --> 00:37:18,375
Take her by the safest road.

400
00:37:18,548 --> 00:37:21,039
A ship lies anchored in the Grey Havens.

401
00:37:21,217 --> 00:37:25,083
It waits to carry her across the sea.

402
00:37:25,261 --> 00:37:28,631
The last journey of Arwen Undomiel.

403
00:38:34,231 --> 00:38:37,316
There is nothing for you here...

404
00:38:37,818 --> 00:38:40,024
only death.

405
00:38:47,325 --> 00:38:48,606
Lady Arwen...

406
00:38:49,535 --> 00:38:51,443
we cannot delay.

407
00:38:53,914 --> 00:38:55,158
My lady!

408
00:39:14,554 --> 00:39:17,175
- Tell me what you have seen.
- Arwen.

409
00:39:17,348 --> 00:39:19,305
You have the gift of foresight.

410
00:39:19,475 --> 00:39:21,266
What did you see?

411
00:39:21,893 --> 00:39:25,227
I looked into your future, and I saw death.

412
00:39:25,772 --> 00:39:27,894
But there is also life.

413
00:39:29,816 --> 00:39:33,860
You saw there was a child. You saw my son.

414
00:39:34,487 --> 00:39:37,023
That future is almost gone.

415
00:39:37,197 --> 00:39:39,189
But it is not lost.

416
00:39:41,785 --> 00:39:43,989
Nothing is certain.

417
00:39:45,703 --> 00:39:48,408
Some things are certain.

418
00:39:52,209 --> 00:39:55,043
If I leave him now...

419
00:39:55,211 --> 00:39:57,831
I will regret it forever.

420
00:39:58,922 --> 00:40:01,246
It is time.

421
00:40:06,511 --> 00:40:10,294
From the ashes a fire shall be woken

422
00:40:10,473 --> 00:40:13,888
A light from the shadow shall spring

423
00:40:14,058 --> 00:40:17,343
Renewed shall be blade that was broken

424
00:40:24,733 --> 00:40:27,936
The crownless again shall be king

425
00:40:31,697 --> 00:40:33,736
Re-forge the sword.

426
00:40:35,439 --> 00:40:36,439
[Sindarin] <i>Ada.</i>
[English] Father.

427
00:41:08,601 --> 00:41:11,305
Your hands are cold.

428
00:41:14,688 --> 00:41:17,809
The life of the Eldar is leaving you.

429
00:41:21,236 --> 00:41:23,145
This was my choice.

430
00:41:23,733 --> 00:41:24,733
[Sindarin] <i>Ada...</i>
[English] Father...

431
00:41:24,989 --> 00:41:27,276
Whether by your will or not...

432
00:41:28,616 --> 00:41:32,910
there is no ship now that can bear me hence.

433
00:42:20,115 --> 00:42:22,950
We've just passed into the realm of Gondor.

434
00:42:34,585 --> 00:42:36,826
Minas Tirith.

435
00:42:37,420 --> 00:42:39,745
City of kings.

436
00:43:11,112 --> 00:43:12,904
Make way!

437
00:43:42,094 --> 00:43:43,922
It's the tree.

438
00:43:44,096 --> 00:43:45,756
Gandalf. Gandalf.

439
00:43:45,931 --> 00:43:48,172
Yes, the White Tree of Gondor.

440
00:43:48,349 --> 00:43:50,176
The tree of the king.

441
00:43:50,351 --> 00:43:53,021
Lord Denethor, however, is not king.

442
00:43:53,188 --> 00:43:55,854
He is a steward only, a caretaker of the throne.

443
00:43:56,605 --> 00:44:00,140
Now listen carefully. Lord
Denethor is Boromir's father.

444
00:44:00,693 --> 00:44:04,476
To give him news of his beloved
son's death would be most unwise.

445
00:44:04,945 --> 00:44:08,397
And do not mention Frodo or the Ring.

446
00:44:09,283 --> 00:44:12,033
And say nothing of Aragorn either.

447
00:44:13,869 --> 00:44:17,736
In fact, it's better if you
don't speak at all, Peregrin Took.

448
00:44:47,897 --> 00:44:54,395
Hail Denethor, son of Ecthelion,
lord and steward of Gondor.

449
00:44:59,905 --> 00:45:04,613
I come with tidings in this
dark hour, and with counsel.

450
00:45:05,576 --> 00:45:08,944
Perhaps you come to explain this.

451
00:45:14,582 --> 00:45:19,125
Perhaps you come to tell me why my son is dead.

452
00:45:33,598 --> 00:45:36,598
Boromir died to save us...

453
00:45:36,768 --> 00:45:38,427
my kinsman and me.

454
00:45:38,601 --> 00:45:42,100
- He fell defending us from many foes.
- Pippin.

455
00:45:47,609 --> 00:45:51,059
I offer you my service, such as it is...

456
00:45:51,612 --> 00:45:53,604
in payment of this debt.

457
00:45:55,781 --> 00:45:59,114
This is my first command to you.

458
00:45:59,827 --> 00:46:03,277
How did you escape and my son did not...

459
00:46:03,620 --> 00:46:05,946
so mighty a man as he was?

460
00:46:06,624 --> 00:46:09,955
The mightiest man may be slain by one arrow...

461
00:46:10,209 --> 00:46:12,118
and Boromir was pierced by many.

462
00:46:16,257 --> 00:46:17,963
Get up.

463
00:46:18,132 --> 00:46:22,758
My lord, there will be a time to grieve for Boromir...

464
00:46:23,219 --> 00:46:24,962
but it is not now.

465
00:46:25,679 --> 00:46:27,885
War is coming.

466
00:46:28,223 --> 00:46:32,635
The enemy is on your doorstep.
As steward, you are charged...

467
00:46:32,811 --> 00:46:36,973
with the defense of this city.
Where are Gondor's armies?

468
00:46:37,147 --> 00:46:42,021
You still have friends. You
are not alone in this fight.

469
00:46:42,192 --> 00:46:46,688
Send word to Theoden of Rohan. Light the beacons.

470
00:46:48,281 --> 00:46:51,815
You think you are wise, Mithrandir.

471
00:46:51,992 --> 00:46:55,028
Yet for all your subtleties, you have not wisdom.

472
00:46:57,162 --> 00:47:01,325
Do you think the eyes of the White Tower are blind?

473
00:47:01,499 --> 00:47:04,584
I have seen more than you know.

474
00:47:04,753 --> 00:47:07,954
With your left hand you would
use me as a shield against Mordor.

475
00:47:08,129 --> 00:47:10,999
And with your right you'd seek to supplant me.

476
00:47:11,173 --> 00:47:14,873
I know who rides with Theoden of Rohan.

477
00:47:15,051 --> 00:47:21,005
Oh, yes. Word has reached my ears
of this Aragorn, son of Arathorn.

478
00:47:21,181 --> 00:47:26,008
And I tell you now, I will not bow
to this Ranger from the North...

479
00:47:26,185 --> 00:47:30,680
last of a ragged house long bereft of lordship.

480
00:47:30,855 --> 00:47:36,690
Authority is not given to you to
deny the return of the king, steward.

481
00:47:36,860 --> 00:47:41,272
The rule of Gondor is mine and no other's.

482
00:47:46,451 --> 00:47:48,242
Come.

483
00:47:56,167 --> 00:47:58,740
All has turned to vain ambition.

484
00:47:58,919 --> 00:48:02,369
He would even use his grief as a cloak.

485
00:48:05,258 --> 00:48:08,042
A thousand years this city has stood.

486
00:48:09,135 --> 00:48:11,542
Now, at the whim of a madman, it will fall.

487
00:48:12,763 --> 00:48:14,969
And the White Tree, the tree of the king...

488
00:48:15,140 --> 00:48:16,682
will never bloom again.

489
00:48:16,849 --> 00:48:20,218
- Why are they still guarding it?
- They guard it because they have hope.

490
00:48:20,395 --> 00:48:23,559
A faint and fading hope that one day it will flower.

491
00:48:23,729 --> 00:48:28,474
That a king will come and this
city will be as it once was...

492
00:48:28,651 --> 00:48:31,566
before it fell into decay.

493
00:48:31,736 --> 00:48:34,986
The old wisdom borne out of the West was forsaken.

494
00:48:35,155 --> 00:48:39,447
Kings made tombs more splendid
than the houses of the living...

495
00:48:39,658 --> 00:48:41,567
and counted the old names of their descent...

496
00:48:41,743 --> 00:48:44,530
dearer than the names of their sons.

497
00:48:44,705 --> 00:48:49,744
Childless lords sat in aged
halls, musing on heraldry...

498
00:48:49,917 --> 00:48:55,254
or in high, cold towers, asking questions of the stars.

499
00:48:55,420 --> 00:48:59,204
And so the people of Gondor fell into ruin.

500
00:49:00,175 --> 00:49:02,500
The line of kings failed.

501
00:49:03,218 --> 00:49:05,590
The White Tree withered.

502
00:49:06,303 --> 00:49:10,467
The rule of Gondor was given over to lesser men.

503
00:49:21,190 --> 00:49:22,435
Mordor.

504
00:49:22,942 --> 00:49:26,606
Yes, there it lies.

505
00:49:27,445 --> 00:49:30,779
This city has dwelt ever in the sight of its shadow.

506
00:49:32,783 --> 00:49:34,442
A storm is coming.

507
00:49:35,118 --> 00:49:38,035
This is not the weather of the world.

508
00:49:38,203 --> 00:49:40,410
This is a device of Sauron's making.

509
00:49:40,581 --> 00:49:44,328
A broil of fume he sends ahead of his host.

510
00:49:44,917 --> 00:49:47,372
The Orcs of Mordor have no love of daylight...

511
00:49:47,545 --> 00:49:49,372
so he covers the face of the sun...

512
00:49:49,547 --> 00:49:53,293
to ease their passage along the road to war.

513
00:49:53,466 --> 00:49:56,751
When the Shadow of Mordor reaches this city...

514
00:49:57,469 --> 00:49:59,176
it will begin.

515
00:50:00,846 --> 00:50:02,424
Well...

516
00:50:02,807 --> 00:50:04,135
Minas Tirith...

517
00:50:06,058 --> 00:50:07,469
very impressive.

518
00:50:07,642 --> 00:50:10,264
- So where are we off to next?
- Oh, it's too late for that, Peregrin.

519
00:50:10,437 --> 00:50:12,644
There's no leaving this city.

520
00:50:14,982 --> 00:50:18,185
Help must come to us.

521
00:50:19,695 --> 00:50:22,363
It must be getting near teatime.

522
00:50:22,529 --> 00:50:26,230
Leastways, it would be in decent
places where there is still teatime.

523
00:50:26,408 --> 00:50:29,990
We're not in decent places.

524
00:50:35,540 --> 00:50:36,785
Mr. Frodo?

525
00:50:39,835 --> 00:50:41,032
What is it?

526
00:50:43,505 --> 00:50:45,876
It's just a feeling.

527
00:50:48,300 --> 00:50:50,458
I don't think I'll be coming back.

528
00:50:54,972 --> 00:50:57,509
Yes, you will. Of course you will.

529
00:50:58,141 --> 00:51:00,014
That's just morbid thinking.

530
00:51:00,477 --> 00:51:02,931
We're going there and back again...

531
00:51:03,103 --> 00:51:05,391
just like Mr. Bilbo.

532
00:51:06,356 --> 00:51:08,479
You'll see.

533
00:51:16,656 --> 00:51:20,272
I think these lands were once
part of the kingdom of Gondor.

534
00:51:24,661 --> 00:51:28,705
Long ago, when there was a king.

535
00:51:49,347 --> 00:51:52,181
Mr. Frodo, look.

536
00:51:53,808 --> 00:51:56,559
The king has got a crown again.

537
00:52:07,695 --> 00:52:11,940
Come on, Hobbits! Mustn't stop now. This way.

538
00:52:28,794 --> 00:52:32,839
So I imagine this is just a ceremonial position.

539
00:52:33,006 --> 00:52:37,252
I mean, they don't actually
expect me to do any fighting.

540
00:52:38,093 --> 00:52:41,343
- Do they?
- You're in the service of the steward now.

541
00:52:41,512 --> 00:52:44,881
You'll have to do as you're told, Peregrin Took.

542
00:52:48,934 --> 00:52:51,425
Ridiculous Hobbit.

543
00:52:52,604 --> 00:52:54,810
Guard of the Citadel.

544
00:53:04,322 --> 00:53:06,148
Thank you.

545
00:53:15,538 --> 00:53:17,780
There's no more stars.

546
00:53:18,290 --> 00:53:19,489
Is it time?

547
00:53:20,668 --> 00:53:22,411
Yes.

548
00:53:25,046 --> 00:53:26,706
It's so quiet.

549
00:53:27,715 --> 00:53:31,961
It's the deep breath before the plunge.

550
00:53:33,136 --> 00:53:36,005
I don't want to be in a battle...

551
00:53:36,848 --> 00:53:41,804
but waiting on the edge of one
I can't escape is even worse.

552
00:53:45,355 --> 00:53:48,971
Is there any hope, Gandalf, for Frodo and Sam?

553
00:53:50,315 --> 00:53:53,435
There never was much hope.

554
00:53:55,403 --> 00:53:57,146
Just a fool's hope.

555
00:54:03,033 --> 00:54:05,820
Our enemy is ready.

556
00:54:05,994 --> 00:54:08,664
His full strength's gathered.

557
00:54:08,831 --> 00:54:12,328
Not only Orcs, but Men as well.

558
00:54:12,500 --> 00:54:15,536
Legions of Haradrim from the south...

559
00:54:15,711 --> 00:54:18,413
mercenaries from the coast.

560
00:54:18,587 --> 00:54:21,160
All will answer Mordor's call.

561
00:54:21,339 --> 00:54:22,881
Come on.

562
00:54:24,009 --> 00:54:27,341
This will be the end of Gondor as we know it.

563
00:54:27,511 --> 00:54:30,880
Here the hammer stroke will fall hardest.

564
00:54:31,849 --> 00:54:36,176
If the river is taken, if the
garrison at Osgiliath falls...

565
00:54:36,351 --> 00:54:40,016
the last defense of this city will be gone.

566
00:54:40,188 --> 00:54:44,232
But we have the White Wizard.
That's got to count for something.

567
00:54:50,111 --> 00:54:51,689
Gandalf?

568
00:54:55,408 --> 00:54:59,072
Sauron has yet to reveal his deadliest servant...

569
00:54:59,536 --> 00:55:03,367
the one who will lead Mordor's armies in war.

570
00:55:03,539 --> 00:55:08,698
The one they say no living man can kill.

571
00:55:09,711 --> 00:55:11,869
The Witch King of Angmar.

572
00:55:12,962 --> 00:55:15,335
You've met him before.

573
00:55:16,007 --> 00:55:18,580
He stabbed Frodo on Weathertop.

574
00:55:25,140 --> 00:55:27,844
He is the lord of the Nazgul...

575
00:55:28,309 --> 00:55:30,764
the greatest of the Nine.

576
00:55:30,935 --> 00:55:34,553
Minas Morgul is his lair.

577
00:55:38,024 --> 00:55:41,558
The Dead City.

578
00:55:41,735 --> 00:55:46,941
Very nasty place. Full of enemies.

579
00:55:54,162 --> 00:55:56,320
Quick. Quick.

580
00:55:56,497 --> 00:56:00,493
They will see. They will see.

581
00:56:09,756 --> 00:56:15,047
Come away. Come away. Look, we have found it.

582
00:56:15,221 --> 00:56:19,086
The way into Mordor.

583
00:56:19,264 --> 00:56:23,594
The secret stair.

584
00:56:24,017 --> 00:56:26,389
Climb.

585
00:56:46,660 --> 00:56:49,411
- No, Mr. Frodo!
- Not that way!

586
00:56:54,250 --> 00:56:57,120
- What's it doing?
- No.

587
00:56:57,294 --> 00:57:00,377
- They're calling me.
- No.

588
00:57:30,027 --> 00:57:32,981
Hide! Hide!

589
00:58:16,522 --> 00:58:19,357
I can feel his blade.

590
00:58:31,032 --> 00:58:33,156
We come to it at last.

591
00:58:34,994 --> 00:58:37,864
The great battle of our time.

592
00:59:17,027 --> 00:59:20,276
Come away, Hobbits. We climb. We must climb.

593
00:59:30,162 --> 00:59:33,162
The board is set.

594
00:59:33,330 --> 00:59:35,869
The pieces are moving.

595
00:59:38,419 --> 00:59:41,088
Up, up, up the stairs we go.

596
00:59:41,254 --> 00:59:43,922
And then it's into the tunnel.

597
00:59:44,089 --> 00:59:47,293
Hey, what's in this tunnel?

598
00:59:47,842 --> 00:59:50,593
You listen to me, and you listen good and proper.

599
00:59:50,761 --> 00:59:53,679
Anything happens to him, you have me to answer to.

600
00:59:53,847 --> 00:59:55,425
One sniff something's not right...

601
00:59:55,600 --> 00:59:58,764
one hair stands up on the back of my head, it's over.

602
00:59:58,975 --> 01:00:01,645
No more slinker. No more stinker.

603
01:00:01,978 --> 01:00:04,599
You're gone. Got it?

604
01:00:05,481 --> 01:00:07,473
I'm watching you.

605
01:00:12,820 --> 01:00:14,812
What was that about?

606
01:00:14,988 --> 01:00:17,395
Nothing. Just clearing something up.

607
01:00:24,037 --> 01:00:26,908
Peregrin Took, my lad, there is a task now to be done.

608
01:00:27,082 --> 01:00:31,658
Another opportunity for one of the
Shire-folk to prove their great worth.

609
01:00:36,505 --> 01:00:38,083
You must not fail me.

610
01:01:12,324 --> 01:01:15,407
It's been very quiet across the river.

611
01:01:15,576 --> 01:01:17,901
The Orcs are lying low.

612
01:01:18,079 --> 01:01:20,071
The garrison may have moved out.

613
01:01:21,207 --> 01:01:23,910
We've sent scouts to Cair Andros.

614
01:01:24,084 --> 01:01:27,368
If the Orcs attack from the
north, we'll have some warning.

615
01:01:52,689 --> 01:01:53,888
Quiet.

616
01:01:57,984 --> 01:01:59,942
We need 10 more.

617
01:02:21,253 --> 01:02:22,795
Kill him!

618
01:02:40,102 --> 01:02:42,507
They're not coming from the north.

619
01:02:43,937 --> 01:02:48,266
To the river. Quick. Quick. Go. Come on.

620
01:02:51,735 --> 01:02:53,312
Faster.

621
01:03:06,455 --> 01:03:08,827
Draw swords.

622
01:04:03,374 --> 01:04:05,947
Hold! Hold them!

623
01:05:26,229 --> 01:05:28,103
What?

624
01:05:40,657 --> 01:05:42,068
Amon Din

625
01:05:47,872 --> 01:05:50,907
The beacon. The beacon of Amon Din is lit.

626
01:05:54,167 --> 01:05:58,378
Hope is kindled.

627
01:07:30,743 --> 01:07:35,120
The beacons of Minas Tirith! The beacons are lit!

628
01:07:36,331 --> 01:07:37,954
Gondor calls for aid.

629
01:07:48,465 --> 01:07:51,382
And Rohan will answer.

630
01:07:51,801 --> 01:07:54,587
Muster the Rohirrim.

631
01:08:09,689 --> 01:08:11,647
Assemble the army at Dunharrow.

632
01:08:11,816 --> 01:08:16,193
As many men as can be found. You have two days.

633
01:08:16,361 --> 01:08:21,651
On the third, we ride for Gondor and war.

634
01:08:22,615 --> 01:08:23,944
- Forward.
- Very good, sir.

635
01:08:24,117 --> 01:08:25,445
- Gamling.
- My lord.

636
01:08:25,618 --> 01:08:27,196
Make haste across the Riddermark.

637
01:08:27,371 --> 01:08:29,492
Summon every able-bodied man to Dunharrow.

638
01:08:29,663 --> 01:08:31,241
I will.

639
01:08:35,335 --> 01:08:38,500
- Will you ride with us?
- Just to the encampment.

640
01:08:38,669 --> 01:08:42,584
It's tradition for the women of
the court to farewell the men.

641
01:08:49,137 --> 01:08:51,047
The men have found their captain.

642
01:08:51,223 --> 01:08:54,554
They will follow you into battle, even to death.

643
01:08:54,724 --> 01:08:56,302
You have given us hope.

644
01:08:59,519 --> 01:09:01,477
Excuse me.

645
01:09:02,814 --> 01:09:04,308
I have a sword.

646
01:09:04,608 --> 01:09:05,983
Please accept it.

647
01:09:07,109 --> 01:09:11,604
I offer you my service, Theoden King.

648
01:09:15,032 --> 01:09:17,107
And gladly I accept it.

649
01:09:18,201 --> 01:09:22,280
You shall be Meriadoc, esquire of Rohan.

650
01:09:27,166 --> 01:09:28,364
Horse-Men.

651
01:09:29,043 --> 01:09:34,665
I wish I could muster a legion of
Dwarves, fully armed and filthy.

652
01:09:35,048 --> 01:09:38,001
Your kinsmen may have no need to ride to war.

653
01:09:38,175 --> 01:09:41,590
I fear war already marches on their own lands.

654
01:10:00,067 --> 01:10:03,517
So it is before the walls of Minas Tirith...

655
01:10:03,695 --> 01:10:07,561
the doom of our time will be decided.

656
01:10:10,158 --> 01:10:15,697
Now is the hour. Riders of Rohan, oaths you have taken.

657
01:10:15,871 --> 01:10:19,404
Now, fulfill them all. To lord and land!

658
01:11:02,490 --> 01:11:04,448
Faramir!

659
01:11:10,746 --> 01:11:14,446
We can't hold them. The city is lost.

660
01:11:15,041 --> 01:11:18,125
Tell the men to break cover. We ride for Minas Tirith.

661
01:11:26,884 --> 01:11:29,125
Nazgul.

662
01:11:31,513 --> 01:11:33,968
Take cover!

663
01:11:34,140 --> 01:11:36,677
Nazgul!

664
01:11:36,849 --> 01:11:40,514
Fall back. Fall back to Minas Tirith!

665
01:11:47,108 --> 01:11:48,982
Fall back!

666
01:11:56,031 --> 01:12:00,609
- Retreat! Retreat!
- Run for your lives!

667
01:12:24,845 --> 01:12:29,174
The age of Men is over.

668
01:12:29,349 --> 01:12:34,970
The time of the Orc has come.

669
01:12:37,355 --> 01:12:39,680
- Keep going.
- It's the Nazgul.

670
01:12:41,316 --> 01:12:43,688
Take cover, my lord!

671
01:12:43,985 --> 01:12:45,314
It's coming!

672
01:12:50,865 --> 01:12:54,234
- It's Mithrandir.
- The White Rider!

673
01:13:34,191 --> 01:13:35,565
Pull!

674
01:13:53,289 --> 01:13:55,696
Mithrandir.

675
01:13:55,874 --> 01:13:57,618
They broke through our defenses.

676
01:13:57,793 --> 01:13:59,998
They've taken the bridge and the west bank.

677
01:14:01,087 --> 01:14:05,249
- Battalions of Orcs are crossing the river.
- It is as the Lord Denethor predicted.

678
01:14:05,423 --> 01:14:09,965
- Long has he foreseen this doom.
- Foreseen and done nothing.

679
01:14:13,346 --> 01:14:15,754
Faramir?

680
01:14:17,683 --> 01:14:21,514
This is not the first Halfling
to have crossed your path.

681
01:14:21,686 --> 01:14:23,891
No.

682
01:14:25,230 --> 01:14:26,772
You've seen Frodo and Sam?

683
01:14:27,649 --> 01:14:31,064
- Where? When?
- In Ithilien.

684
01:14:31,235 --> 01:14:33,310
Not two days ago.

685
01:14:33,778 --> 01:14:38,237
Gandalf, they're taking the road to the Morgul Vale.

686
01:14:38,949 --> 01:14:41,570
And then the pass of Cirith Ungol.

687
01:14:43,787 --> 01:14:46,158
What does that mean?

688
01:14:46,330 --> 01:14:51,239
- What's wrong?
- Faramir, tell me everything.

689
01:14:51,417 --> 01:14:53,456
Tell me all you know.

690
01:14:54,628 --> 01:14:58,043
This is how you would serve your city?

691
01:14:58,215 --> 01:15:01,499
You would risk its utter ruin?

692
01:15:02,550 --> 01:15:04,127
I did what I judged to be right.

693
01:15:04,843 --> 01:15:07,844
What you judged to be right.

694
01:15:08,472 --> 01:15:14,344
You sent the Ring of Power into Mordor
in the hands of a witless Halfling.

695
01:15:18,312 --> 01:15:23,140
It should have been brought back
to the Citadel to be kept safe.

696
01:15:24,777 --> 01:15:26,318
Hidden.

697
01:15:26,736 --> 01:15:29,488
Dark and deep in the vaults...

698
01:15:29,655 --> 01:15:31,814
not to be used.

699
01:15:35,993 --> 01:15:40,868
Unless at the uttermost end of need.

700
01:15:41,331 --> 01:15:43,370
I would not use the Ring.

701
01:15:43,541 --> 01:15:46,626
Not if Minas Tirith were falling
in ruin and I alone could save her.

702
01:15:46,960 --> 01:15:51,786
Ever you desire to appear lordly and gracious...

703
01:15:51,964 --> 01:15:54,206
as a king of old.

704
01:15:56,009 --> 01:15:59,757
Boromir would have remembered his father's need.

705
01:16:00,179 --> 01:16:02,634
He would have brought me a kingly gift.

706
01:16:02,847 --> 01:16:05,384
Boromir would not have brought the Ring.

707
01:16:05,808 --> 01:16:08,927
He would have stretched out his hand to
this thing and taken it. He would've fallen.

708
01:16:09,102 --> 01:16:11,344
- You know nothing of this matter!
- He would have kept it for his own.

709
01:16:13,231 --> 01:16:15,389
And when he returned...

710
01:16:16,524 --> 01:16:18,184
you would not have known your son.

711
01:16:18,359 --> 01:16:20,896
Boromir was loyal to me!

712
01:16:21,069 --> 01:16:23,642
Not some wizard's pupil!

713
01:16:31,786 --> 01:16:33,114
Father?

714
01:16:45,798 --> 01:16:47,706
My son.

715
01:17:13,945 --> 01:17:15,319
Leave me.

716
01:17:48,887 --> 01:17:51,425
Careful, master. Careful.

717
01:17:51,765 --> 01:17:54,682
Very far to fall.

718
01:17:57,186 --> 01:18:01,099
Very dangerous are the stairs.

719
01:18:03,774 --> 01:18:06,312
Come, master.

720
01:18:12,115 --> 01:18:15,280
Come to Smeagol.

721
01:18:21,621 --> 01:18:23,115
Mr. Frodo.

722
01:18:24,124 --> 01:18:25,666
Get back, you!

723
01:18:25,834 --> 01:18:28,039
Don't touch him!

724
01:18:32,171 --> 01:18:35,005
Why does he hates poor Smeagol?

725
01:18:35,173 --> 01:18:38,874
What has Smeagol ever done to him?

726
01:18:39,052 --> 01:18:41,424
Master?

727
01:18:42,220 --> 01:18:45,671
Master carries heavy burden.

728
01:18:45,848 --> 01:18:51,268
Smeagol knows. Heavy, heavy burden.

729
01:18:51,436 --> 01:18:54,686
Fat one cannot know.

730
01:18:56,733 --> 01:18:59,482
Smeagol look after master.

731
01:19:00,693 --> 01:19:02,900
He wants it.

732
01:19:03,070 --> 01:19:07,612
He needs it. Smeagol sees it in his eye.

733
01:19:07,782 --> 01:19:13,238
Very soon he will ask you for it. You will see.

734
01:19:13,412 --> 01:19:17,278
The fat one will take it from you.

735
01:19:24,503 --> 01:19:28,833
Send forth all legions.

736
01:19:29,007 --> 01:19:33,051
Do not stop the attack until the city is taken.

737
01:19:33,761 --> 01:19:36,881
Slay them all.

738
01:19:38,556 --> 01:19:44,344
- What of the wizard?
- I will break him.

739
01:19:47,688 --> 01:19:50,095
Where are Theoden's riders?

740
01:19:50,273 --> 01:19:52,846
Will Rohan's army come?

741
01:19:53,025 --> 01:19:55,267
Mithrandir.

742
01:19:56,320 --> 01:20:00,186
Courage is the best defense that you have now.

743
01:20:04,994 --> 01:20:07,698
What were you thinking, Peregrin Took?

744
01:20:09,788 --> 01:20:15,493
What service can a Hobbit
offer such a great lord of Men?

745
01:20:15,668 --> 01:20:17,162
It was well-done.

746
01:20:20,338 --> 01:20:24,382
A generous deed should not
be checked with cold counsel.

747
01:20:25,133 --> 01:20:27,672
You are to join the tower guard.

748
01:20:28,220 --> 01:20:31,219
I didn't think they would find
any livery that would fit me.

749
01:20:31,389 --> 01:20:33,843
Once belonged to a young boy of the city.

750
01:20:34,015 --> 01:20:35,557
A very foolish one...

751
01:20:35,725 --> 01:20:39,971
who wasted many hours slaying dragons
instead of attending to his studies.

752
01:20:40,145 --> 01:20:42,897
- This was yours?
- Yes, it was mine.

753
01:20:43,065 --> 01:20:44,855
My father had it made for me.

754
01:20:45,900 --> 01:20:47,229
Well...

755
01:20:47,402 --> 01:20:49,392
I'm taller than you were then.

756
01:20:49,569 --> 01:20:52,903
Though I'm not likely to grow anymore, except sideways.

757
01:20:55,866 --> 01:20:57,905
Never fitted me either.

758
01:20:58,075 --> 01:21:00,911
Boromir was always the soldier.

759
01:21:03,914 --> 01:21:06,321
They were so alike, he and my father.

760
01:21:08,418 --> 01:21:10,043
Proud.

761
01:21:10,211 --> 01:21:11,409
Stubborn even.

762
01:21:13,171 --> 01:21:14,665
But strong.

763
01:21:16,173 --> 01:21:19,339
I think you have strength of a different kind.

764
01:21:19,968 --> 01:21:22,423
And one day your father will see it.

765
01:21:26,599 --> 01:21:30,381
Here do I swear fealty and service to Gondor...

766
01:21:30,559 --> 01:21:32,054
in peace or war...

767
01:21:32,687 --> 01:21:35,141
in living or dying...

768
01:21:36,523 --> 01:21:37,767
from...

769
01:21:40,443 --> 01:21:43,228
From this hour henceforth...

770
01:21:43,402 --> 01:21:45,311
until my lord release me...

771
01:21:46,822 --> 01:21:49,028
or death take me.

772
01:21:49,616 --> 01:21:52,106
And I shall not forget it...

773
01:21:52,284 --> 01:21:55,654
nor fail to reward that which is given.

774
01:22:03,252 --> 01:22:05,540
Fealty with love.

775
01:22:06,628 --> 01:22:08,289
Valor with honor.

776
01:22:09,882 --> 01:22:13,214
Disloyalty with vengeance.

777
01:22:21,850 --> 01:22:25,929
I do not think we should so lightly
abandon the outer defenses...

778
01:22:26,103 --> 01:22:28,854
defenses that your brother long held intact.

779
01:22:29,021 --> 01:22:31,511
- What would you have me do?
- I will not yield...

780
01:22:31,690 --> 01:22:34,477
the river in Pelennor unfought.

781
01:22:34,651 --> 01:22:36,311
Osgiliath must be retaken.

782
01:22:36,486 --> 01:22:38,525
My lord, Osgiliath is overrun.

783
01:22:39,196 --> 01:22:41,982
Much must be risked in war.

784
01:22:44,617 --> 01:22:48,566
Is there a captain here who still
has the courage to do his lord's will?

785
01:22:54,791 --> 01:22:58,040
You wish now that our places had been exchanged...

786
01:22:59,003 --> 01:23:01,837
that I had died and Boromir had lived.

787
01:23:05,258 --> 01:23:07,001
Yes.

788
01:23:07,677 --> 01:23:09,882
I wish that.

789
01:23:18,267 --> 01:23:20,758
Since you were robbed of Boromir...

790
01:23:22,605 --> 01:23:25,522
I will do what I can in his stead.

791
01:23:33,696 --> 01:23:38,156
If I should return, think better of me, Father.

792
01:23:40,244 --> 01:23:43,860
That will depend on the manner of your return.

793
01:25:07,145 --> 01:25:09,469
What are you up to?

794
01:25:09,646 --> 01:25:10,890
Sneaking off, are we?

795
01:25:11,606 --> 01:25:13,432
Sneaking?

796
01:25:14,441 --> 01:25:16,598
Sneaking?

797
01:25:18,027 --> 01:25:21,193
Fat Hobbit is always so polite.

798
01:25:21,364 --> 01:25:26,438
Smeagol shows them secret ways
that nobody else could find...

799
01:25:26,617 --> 01:25:28,775
and they say "sneak."

800
01:25:29,411 --> 01:25:31,984
Sneak?

801
01:25:32,621 --> 01:25:35,326
Very nice friend. Oh, yes, my precious.

802
01:25:35,499 --> 01:25:38,121
- Very nice, very nice.
- All right. All right!

803
01:25:39,377 --> 01:25:41,582
You just startled me is all.

804
01:25:42,087 --> 01:25:43,914
What were you doing?

805
01:25:45,549 --> 01:25:47,670
Sneaking.

806
01:25:48,050 --> 01:25:51,135
Fine. Have it your own way.

807
01:25:53,389 --> 01:25:55,878
I'm sorry to wake you, Mr. Frodo.

808
01:25:56,265 --> 01:25:58,221
We have to be moving on.

809
01:26:03,395 --> 01:26:04,973
It's dark still.

810
01:26:05,147 --> 01:26:07,353
It's always dark here.

811
01:26:11,610 --> 01:26:13,518
It's gone!

812
01:26:14,738 --> 01:26:17,608
- The Elven bread.
- What?

813
01:26:17,782 --> 01:26:19,240
That's all we have left.

814
01:26:23,328 --> 01:26:25,819
He took it. He must have!

815
01:26:26,329 --> 01:26:29,580
Smeagol? No, no, not poor Smeagol.

816
01:26:29,749 --> 01:26:32,667
Smeagol hates nasty Elf bread.

817
01:26:32,836 --> 01:26:36,001
You're a lying rat! What did you do with it?!

818
01:26:36,171 --> 01:26:37,713
He doesn't eat it.

819
01:26:38,716 --> 01:26:41,040
- He can't have taken it.
- Look.

820
01:26:42,091 --> 01:26:43,919
What's this?

821
01:26:46,596 --> 01:26:49,929
Crumbs on his jacketses. He took it!

822
01:26:50,640 --> 01:26:52,301
He took it.

823
01:26:53,143 --> 01:26:57,353
I seen him. He's always stuffing
his face when master's not looking.

824
01:26:57,522 --> 01:26:59,312
That's a filthy lie!

825
01:26:59,480 --> 01:27:01,687
You stinking, two-faced sneak!

826
01:27:01,857 --> 01:27:03,103
- Sam!
- Call me...

827
01:27:03,276 --> 01:27:04,521
Stop it!

828
01:27:05,528 --> 01:27:06,725
Sam!

829
01:27:08,029 --> 01:27:11,646
- I'll kill him!
- Sam! No!

830
01:27:12,700 --> 01:27:18,238
Oh, my... I'm sorry. I didn't mean it
to go so far. I was just so... So angry.

831
01:27:18,412 --> 01:27:20,535
Here, just... Let's
just rest a bit.

832
01:27:20,706 --> 01:27:22,781
- I'm all right.
- No.

833
01:27:22,957 --> 01:27:26,041
No, you're not all right. You're exhausted.

834
01:27:26,209 --> 01:27:28,332
It's that Gollum.

835
01:27:28,503 --> 01:27:30,211
It's this place.

836
01:27:30,379 --> 01:27:32,952
It's that thing around your neck.

837
01:27:36,469 --> 01:27:37,748
I could help a bit.

838
01:27:37,927 --> 01:27:40,595
I could carry it for a while.

839
01:27:40,763 --> 01:27:42,506
Carry it for a while.

840
01:27:42,681 --> 01:27:43,926
I could carry it... I could carry it.

841
01:27:44,558 --> 01:27:50,013
Share the load... Share the
load... the load... the load.

842
01:27:50,187 --> 01:27:51,386
Get away!

843
01:27:51,564 --> 01:27:53,139
I don't want to keep it.

844
01:27:56,734 --> 01:27:58,725
I just want to help.

845
01:28:00,778 --> 01:28:03,400
See? See?

846
01:28:03,572 --> 01:28:06,988
He wants it for himself.

847
01:28:07,160 --> 01:28:08,865
Shut up, you!

848
01:28:09,409 --> 01:28:11,236
Go away! Get out of here!

849
01:28:11,411 --> 01:28:13,238
No, Sam.

850
01:28:13,413 --> 01:28:14,658
It's you.

851
01:28:18,876 --> 01:28:20,583
I'm sorry, Sam.

852
01:28:22,254 --> 01:28:23,628
But he's a liar.

853
01:28:23,796 --> 01:28:26,464
He's poisoned you against me.

854
01:28:27,883 --> 01:28:29,791
You can't help me anymore.

855
01:28:31,761 --> 01:28:33,633
You don't mean that.

856
01:28:36,140 --> 01:28:37,930
Go home.

857
01:29:57,953 --> 01:29:59,743
Faramir!

858
01:29:59,912 --> 01:30:01,821
Faramir!

859
01:30:03,332 --> 01:30:05,372
Your father's will has turned to madness.

860
01:30:06,542 --> 01:30:08,581
Do not throw away your life so rashly.

861
01:30:09,336 --> 01:30:11,661
Where does my allegiance lie if not here?

862
01:30:12,297 --> 01:30:15,214
This is the city of the Men of Numenor.

863
01:30:15,841 --> 01:30:18,628
I will gladly give my life to defend her beauty...

864
01:30:18,802 --> 01:30:22,005
her memory, her wisdom.

865
01:30:24,389 --> 01:30:27,805
Your father loves you, Faramir.

866
01:30:28,518 --> 01:30:31,518
He will remember it before the end.

867
01:31:41,116 --> 01:31:42,657
Can you sing, Master Hobbit?

868
01:31:45,640 --> 01:31:47,134
Well...

869
01:31:47,684 --> 01:31:49,307
yes.

870
01:31:50,019 --> 01:31:53,766
At least, well enough for my own people.

871
01:31:55,398 --> 01:31:57,804
But we have no songs for great halls...

872
01:31:58,858 --> 01:32:00,103
and evil times.

873
01:32:00,943 --> 01:32:04,110
And why should your songs be unfit for my halls?

874
01:32:06,906 --> 01:32:08,317
Come, sing me a song.

875
01:32:19,376 --> 01:32:22,707
Home is behind

876
01:32:22,876 --> 01:32:26,625
The world ahead

877
01:32:29,048 --> 01:32:34,883
And there are many paths to tread

878
01:32:36,678 --> 01:32:40,213
Through shadow

879
01:32:40,390 --> 01:32:44,553
To the edge of night

880
01:32:46,228 --> 01:32:51,305
Until the stars are all alight

881
01:32:54,318 --> 01:32:58,646
Mist and shadow

882
01:32:58,822 --> 01:33:03,114
Cloud and shade

883
01:33:05,493 --> 01:33:08,826
All shall fade

884
01:33:11,206 --> 01:33:15,203
All shall

885
01:33:20,964 --> 01:33:23,336
Fade

886
01:33:47,734 --> 01:33:51,185
March! March!

887
01:33:51,362 --> 01:33:56,568
March! March! March!

888
01:34:00,037 --> 01:34:02,362
Make way for the king.

889
01:34:03,872 --> 01:34:05,863
Make way.

890
01:34:08,333 --> 01:34:10,373
The king is here.

891
01:34:12,337 --> 01:34:13,961
My lord.

892
01:34:15,215 --> 01:34:17,171
Hail to you, sire.

893
01:34:17,634 --> 01:34:18,829
Grimbold, how many?

894
01:34:19,008 --> 01:34:21,463
I bring 500 men from the Westfold, my lord.

895
01:34:22,428 --> 01:34:25,097
We have 300 more from Fenmarch, Theoden King.

896
01:34:26,223 --> 01:34:30,171
- Where are the riders from Snowborn?
- None have come, my lord.

897
01:34:47,240 --> 01:34:49,362
Six thousand spears.

898
01:34:50,407 --> 01:34:52,400
Less than half of what I'd hoped for.

899
01:34:52,701 --> 01:34:56,070
Six thousand will not be enough
to break the lines of Mordor.

900
01:34:58,831 --> 01:35:00,574
More will come.

901
01:35:00,958 --> 01:35:03,911
Every hour lost hastens Gondor's defeat.

902
01:35:04,085 --> 01:35:06,657
We have till dawn, then we must ride.

903
01:35:26,144 --> 01:35:28,469
The horses are restless...

904
01:35:28,647 --> 01:35:30,140
and the men are quiet.

905
01:35:30,606 --> 01:35:33,724
They grow nervous in the shadow of the mountain.

906
01:35:36,194 --> 01:35:38,066
That road there...

907
01:35:38,987 --> 01:35:41,063
where does that lead?

908
01:35:41,823 --> 01:35:45,654
It is the road to the Dimholt,
the door under the mountain.

909
01:35:46,368 --> 01:35:49,368
None who venture there ever return.

910
01:35:50,579 --> 01:35:52,453
That mountain is evil.

911
01:36:15,391 --> 01:36:17,216
Aragorn.

912
01:36:17,975 --> 01:36:19,884
Let's find some food.

913
01:36:36,365 --> 01:36:37,776
There.

914
01:36:38,742 --> 01:36:41,742
A true esquire of Rohan.

915
01:36:45,373 --> 01:36:47,364
I'm ready.

916
01:36:48,958 --> 01:36:50,237
Sorry.

917
01:36:50,418 --> 01:36:52,658
It isn't all that dangerous.

918
01:36:53,170 --> 01:36:55,495
It's not even sharp.

919
01:36:56,172 --> 01:36:59,588
Well, that's no good. You won't
kill many Orcs with a blunt blade.

920
01:36:59,759 --> 01:37:01,253
Come on.

921
01:37:05,428 --> 01:37:07,920
To the smithy. Go!

922
01:37:09,391 --> 01:37:11,928
You should not encourage him.

923
01:37:12,101 --> 01:37:14,556
You should not doubt him.

924
01:37:14,729 --> 01:37:18,013
I do not doubt his heart, only the reach of his arm.

925
01:37:20,733 --> 01:37:22,310
Why should Merry be left behind?

926
01:37:22,484 --> 01:37:25,105
He has as much cause to go to war as you.

927
01:37:27,280 --> 01:37:30,445
Why can he not fight for those he loves?

928
01:37:33,701 --> 01:37:36,701
You know as little of war as that Hobbit.

929
01:37:37,954 --> 01:37:40,030
When the fear takes him...

930
01:37:40,206 --> 01:37:45,247
and the blood and the screams and
the horror of battle take hold...

931
01:37:45,627 --> 01:37:47,784
do you think he would stand and fight?

932
01:37:50,339 --> 01:37:51,963
He would flee.

933
01:37:52,132 --> 01:37:54,171
And he would be right to do so.

934
01:37:56,386 --> 01:38:00,335
War is the province of Men, Eowyn.

935
01:38:35,999 --> 01:38:39,699
I choose a mortal life.

936
01:38:42,630 --> 01:38:45,499
I wish I could've seen him...

937
01:38:46,632 --> 01:38:49,337
one last time.

938
01:39:00,518 --> 01:39:01,929
Sir?

939
01:39:03,771 --> 01:39:06,344
King Theoden awaits you, my lord.

940
01:39:27,122 --> 01:39:29,079
I take my leave.

941
01:39:43,718 --> 01:39:44,963
My lord Elrond.

942
01:39:45,553 --> 01:39:49,052
I come on behalf of one whom I love.

943
01:39:52,141 --> 01:39:54,134
Arwen is dying.

944
01:39:58,938 --> 01:40:02,982
She will not long survive the
evil that now spreads from Mordor.

945
01:40:03,734 --> 01:40:07,102
The light of the Evenstar is failing.

946
01:40:07,278 --> 01:40:11,276
As Sauron's power grows, her strength wanes.

947
01:40:11,449 --> 01:40:15,195
Arwen's life is now tied to the fate of the Ring.

948
01:40:15,951 --> 01:40:18,524
The Shadow is upon us, Aragorn.

949
01:40:18,913 --> 01:40:20,572
The end has come.

950
01:40:20,956 --> 01:40:23,576
It will not be our end, but his.

951
01:40:24,333 --> 01:40:27,916
You ride to war, but not to victory.

952
01:40:28,919 --> 01:40:32,584
Sauron's armies march on Minas Tirith, this you know.

953
01:40:32,756 --> 01:40:37,168
But in secret he sends another force
which will attack from the river.

954
01:40:37,635 --> 01:40:41,051
A fleet of Corsair ships sails from the south.

955
01:40:41,681 --> 01:40:43,756
They'll be in the city in two days.

956
01:40:44,265 --> 01:40:47,099
You're outnumbered, Aragorn.

957
01:40:47,809 --> 01:40:49,933
You need more men.

958
01:40:50,312 --> 01:40:52,056
There are none.

959
01:40:53,814 --> 01:40:57,728
There are those who dwell in the mountain.

960
01:41:06,741 --> 01:41:08,899
Murderers...

961
01:41:09,076 --> 01:41:10,487
traitors.

962
01:41:12,955 --> 01:41:15,112
You would call upon them to fight?

963
01:41:15,289 --> 01:41:16,866
They believe in nothing.

964
01:41:17,040 --> 01:41:19,163
They answer to no one.

965
01:41:19,334 --> 01:41:22,418
They will answer to the king of Gondor.

966
01:41:29,550 --> 01:41:34,674
Anduril, the Flame of the West,
forged from the shards of Narsil.

967
01:41:48,982 --> 01:41:53,395
Sauron will not have forgotten the Sword of Elendil.

968
01:42:07,455 --> 01:42:12,199
The blade that was broken shall return to Minas Tirith.

969
01:42:12,376 --> 01:42:14,782
The man who can wield the power of this sword...

970
01:42:14,960 --> 01:42:18,826
can summon to him an army more
deadly than any that walks this earth.

971
01:42:20,673 --> 01:42:22,831
Put aside the Ranger.

972
01:42:23,009 --> 01:42:26,342
Become who you were born to be.

973
01:42:26,512 --> 01:42:28,503
Take the Dimholt road.

974
01:42:32,438 --> 01:42:34,823
[Sindarin] <i>Ónen i-Estel Edain.</i>
[English] I gave hope to Men.

975
01:42:38,569 --> 01:42:39,669
[Sindarin] <i>Ú-chebin...</i>
[English] I have kept...

976
01:42:41,255 --> 01:42:42,469
[Sindarin] <i>...Estel anim.</i>
[English] ...no hope for me.

977
01:42:54,533 --> 01:42:56,194
Why are you doing this?

978
01:42:56,660 --> 01:42:59,861
The war lies to the east. You
cannot leave on the eve of battle.

979
01:43:02,289 --> 01:43:04,364
You cannot abandon the men.

980
01:43:05,667 --> 01:43:07,243
Eowyn...

981
01:43:07,417 --> 01:43:09,624
We need you here.

982
01:43:10,754 --> 01:43:12,627
Why have you come?

983
01:43:14,297 --> 01:43:16,254
Do you not know?

984
01:43:25,557 --> 01:43:28,557
It is but a shadow and a thought that you love.

985
01:43:32,478 --> 01:43:34,887
I cannot give you what you seek.

986
01:43:48,408 --> 01:43:52,322
I have wished you joy since first I saw you.

987
01:44:11,467 --> 01:44:13,755
Just where do you think you're off to?

988
01:44:13,927 --> 01:44:15,256
Not this time.

989
01:44:15,429 --> 01:44:17,634
This time you must stay, Gimli.

990
01:44:20,350 --> 01:44:23,184
Have you learned nothing of
the stubbornness of Dwarves?

991
01:44:23,353 --> 01:44:27,015
You might as well accept it.
We're going with you, laddie.

992
01:44:49,330 --> 01:44:51,488
- What's happening?
- Where is he going?

993
01:44:51,832 --> 01:44:53,706
Where's he going?

994
01:44:56,293 --> 01:44:58,332
I don't understand.

995
01:45:02,758 --> 01:45:04,548
Lord Aragorn!

996
01:45:04,967 --> 01:45:07,671
Why does he leave on the eve of battle?

997
01:45:08,888 --> 01:45:10,963
He leaves because there is no hope.

998
01:45:11,639 --> 01:45:13,761
He leaves because he must.

999
01:45:13,931 --> 01:45:15,640
Too few have come.

1000
01:45:15,809 --> 01:45:17,967
We cannot defeat the armies of Mordor.

1001
01:45:20,479 --> 01:45:22,139
No...

1002
01:45:22,564 --> 01:45:23,809
we cannot.

1003
01:45:26,692 --> 01:45:30,475
But we will meet them in battle nonetheless.

1004
01:45:44,914 --> 01:45:46,658
I have left instruction.

1005
01:45:49,335 --> 01:45:52,584
The people are to follow your rule in my stead.

1006
01:45:59,175 --> 01:46:01,417
Take up my seat in the Golden Hall.

1007
01:46:02,679 --> 01:46:05,514
Long may you defend Edoras...

1008
01:46:05,682 --> 01:46:08,006
if the battle goes ill.

1009
01:46:09,100 --> 01:46:12,515
What other duty would you have me do, my lord?

1010
01:46:14,730 --> 01:46:16,686
Duty?

1011
01:46:18,858 --> 01:46:20,186
No.

1012
01:46:28,490 --> 01:46:30,613
I would have you smile again...

1013
01:46:34,036 --> 01:46:39,030
not grieve for those whose time has come.

1014
01:46:43,877 --> 01:46:47,375
You shall live to see these days renewed...

1015
01:46:51,717 --> 01:46:54,466
and no more despair.

1016
01:47:00,682 --> 01:47:04,381
What kind of army would linger in such a place?

1017
01:47:04,560 --> 01:47:06,387
One that is cursed.

1018
01:47:08,356 --> 01:47:10,891
Long ago, the Men of the Mountains swore an oath...

1019
01:47:11,314 --> 01:47:14,066
to the last king of Gondor...

1020
01:47:14,651 --> 01:47:16,228
to come to his aid...

1021
01:47:16,402 --> 01:47:18,109
to fight.

1022
01:47:18,612 --> 01:47:20,770
But when the time came...

1023
01:47:21,407 --> 01:47:24,026
when Gondor's need was dire...

1024
01:47:24,199 --> 01:47:26,072
they fled...

1025
01:47:26,242 --> 01:47:29,612
vanishing into the darkness of the mountain.

1026
01:47:30,663 --> 01:47:32,988
And so Isildur cursed them...

1027
01:47:34,541 --> 01:47:38,408
never to rest until they had fulfilled their pledge.

1028
01:47:42,714 --> 01:47:45,880
Who shall call them from the grey twilight?

1029
01:47:46,342 --> 01:47:48,584
The forgotten people.

1030
01:47:48,761 --> 01:47:51,251
The heir of him to whom the oath they swore.

1031
01:47:51,722 --> 01:47:53,594
From the north shall he come.

1032
01:47:54,098 --> 01:47:55,757
Need shall drive him.

1033
01:47:56,851 --> 01:48:00,348
He shall pass the door to the Paths of the Dead.

1034
01:48:18,826 --> 01:48:22,111
The very warmth of my blood seems stolen away.

1035
01:48:27,666 --> 01:48:29,622
The way is shut.

1036
01:48:30,376 --> 01:48:32,333
It was made by those who are dead.

1037
01:48:32,961 --> 01:48:35,203
And the Dead keep it.

1038
01:48:35,756 --> 01:48:37,297
The way is shut.

1039
01:48:48,641 --> 01:48:50,135
Brego!

1040
01:48:53,644 --> 01:48:56,348
I do not fear death.

1041
01:49:08,655 --> 01:49:11,063
Well, this is a thing unheard-of.

1042
01:49:11,241 --> 01:49:15,903
An Elf will go underground where a Dwarf dare not?

1043
01:49:16,078 --> 01:49:17,406
Oh.

1044
01:49:17,579 --> 01:49:20,414
Oh, I'd never hear the end of it.

1045
01:49:35,427 --> 01:49:37,668
We must ride light and swift.

1046
01:49:37,845 --> 01:49:39,587
It is a long road ahead.

1047
01:49:39,762 --> 01:49:42,847
And man and beast must reach the
end with the strength to fight.

1048
01:49:48,353 --> 01:49:51,354
Little Hobbits do not belong in war, Master Meriadoc.

1049
01:49:51,689 --> 01:49:53,681
All my friends have gone to battle.

1050
01:49:53,857 --> 01:49:55,730
I would be ashamed to be left behind.

1051
01:49:55,900 --> 01:49:58,023
It is a three-day gallop to Minas Tirith.

1052
01:49:58,194 --> 01:50:00,566
And none of my riders can bear you as a burden.

1053
01:50:01,572 --> 01:50:03,694
I want to fight.

1054
01:50:04,199 --> 01:50:06,191
I will say no more.

1055
01:50:23,005 --> 01:50:24,962
Ride with me.

1056
01:50:26,425 --> 01:50:27,834
My lady.

1057
01:50:28,008 --> 01:50:30,380
Form up! Move out!

1058
01:50:30,553 --> 01:50:33,756
Form up! Move out!

1059
01:50:36,848 --> 01:50:38,046
Ride!

1060
01:50:38,225 --> 01:50:41,179
Ride now to Gondor!

1061
01:50:50,404 --> 01:50:52,003
[Black Speech] <i> Katmuda! </i>
[English]  Death to men!

1062
01:50:53,527 --> 01:50:54,827
[Black Speech] <i> Katmuda! </i>
[English]  Death to men!

1063
01:50:54,828 --> 01:50:55,428
[Black Speech] <i> Gorosh! </i>
[English]  Louder!

1064
01:50:55,429 --> 01:50:56,729
[Black Speech] <i> Katmuda! </i>
[English]  Death to men!

1065
01:50:56,730 --> 01:50:57,230
[Black Speech] <i> Gorosh! </i>
[English]  Louder!

1066
01:50:57,231 --> 01:50:58,530
[Black Speech] <i> Katmuda! </i>
[English]  Death to men!

1067
01:50:58,531 --> 01:51:00,031
[Black Speech] <i> Gorosh chadar! </i>
[English]  Loud enough!

1068
01:51:22,801 --> 01:51:24,544
What is it?

1069
01:51:24,719 --> 01:51:26,261
What do you see?

1070
01:51:26,512 --> 01:51:28,635
I see shapes of men.

1071
01:51:31,308 --> 01:51:32,683
And of horses.

1072
01:51:33,435 --> 01:51:34,633
Where?

1073
01:51:34,811 --> 01:51:37,763
Pale banners like shreds of cloud.

1074
01:51:40,190 --> 01:51:42,395
Spears rise...

1075
01:51:43,025 --> 01:51:46,476
like winter-thickets through a shroud of mist.

1076
01:51:47,737 --> 01:51:49,895
The Dead are following.

1077
01:51:51,115 --> 01:51:52,609
They have been summoned.

1078
01:51:53,284 --> 01:51:55,109
The Dead?

1079
01:51:55,493 --> 01:51:57,201
Summoned?

1080
01:51:57,620 --> 01:51:59,494
I knew that.

1081
01:52:02,832 --> 01:52:04,576
Very good.

1082
01:52:05,293 --> 01:52:07,368
Very good! Legolas!

1083
01:52:45,324 --> 01:52:46,734
Do not look down.

1084
01:53:39,324 --> 01:53:44,448
Who enters my domain?

1085
01:53:48,207 --> 01:53:50,411
One who will have your allegiance.

1086
01:53:53,375 --> 01:53:58,714
The Dead do not suffer the living to pass.

1087
01:53:59,048 --> 01:54:01,716
You will suffer me.

1088
01:54:25,233 --> 01:54:28,603
The way is shut.

1089
01:54:29,780 --> 01:54:34,238
It was made by those who are dead.

1090
01:54:34,616 --> 01:54:38,778
And the Dead keep it.

1091
01:54:47,918 --> 01:54:51,002
The way is shut.

1092
01:54:52,756 --> 01:54:55,376
Now you must die.

1093
01:54:59,261 --> 01:55:02,096
I summon you to fulfill your oath.

1094
01:55:02,430 --> 01:55:07,386
None but the king of Gondor may command me.

1095
01:55:12,980 --> 01:55:15,137
That line was broken.

1096
01:55:17,776 --> 01:55:19,980
It has been remade.

1097
01:55:27,907 --> 01:55:29,450
Fight for us...

1098
01:55:29,618 --> 01:55:32,156
and regain your honor.

1099
01:55:36,330 --> 01:55:37,659
What say you?

1100
01:55:49,882 --> 01:55:51,424
What say you?

1101
01:55:52,176 --> 01:55:53,968
You waste your time, Aragorn.

1102
01:55:54,137 --> 01:55:57,303
They had no honor in life, they have none now in death.

1103
01:55:57,806 --> 01:56:00,297
I am Isildur's heir.

1104
01:56:00,851 --> 01:56:02,806
Fight for me...

1105
01:56:03,393 --> 01:56:06,975
and I will hold your oaths fulfilled.

1106
01:56:10,900 --> 01:56:12,857
What say you?

1107
01:56:20,782 --> 01:56:22,988
You have my word!

1108
01:56:23,283 --> 01:56:27,282
Fight, and I will release you from this living death!

1109
01:56:28,748 --> 01:56:30,241
What say you?!

1110
01:56:33,542 --> 01:56:36,496
Stand, you traitors!

1111
01:57:03,439 --> 01:57:04,471
Out!

1112
01:57:25,832 --> 01:57:27,410
Legolas!

1113
01:57:28,544 --> 01:57:29,741
Run!

1114
01:58:36,053 --> 01:58:38,128
We fight.

1115
01:58:48,480 --> 01:58:51,052
Open the gate! Quick!

1116
01:59:22,090 --> 01:59:24,081
Quick! Hurry!

1117
01:59:37,850 --> 01:59:39,475
Faramir!

1118
01:59:40,479 --> 01:59:43,728
Say not that he has fallen.

1119
01:59:44,899 --> 01:59:46,440
They were outnumbered.

1120
01:59:46,857 --> 01:59:48,435
None survived.

1121
01:59:49,151 --> 01:59:51,144
Fear.

1122
01:59:51,696 --> 01:59:54,898
The city is rank with it.

1123
01:59:57,242 --> 01:59:59,696
Let us ease their pain.

1124
01:59:59,952 --> 02:00:01,694
Release the prisoners.

1125
02:00:01,869 --> 02:00:03,827
Catapults!

1126
02:00:17,173 --> 02:00:20,624
My sons are spent.

1127
02:00:21,677 --> 02:00:24,594
My line has ended.

1128
02:00:27,432 --> 02:00:28,843
He's alive!

1129
02:00:29,016 --> 02:00:32,182
The House of Stewards has failed.

1130
02:00:32,352 --> 02:00:33,809
He needs medicine, my lord.

1131
02:00:34,854 --> 02:00:37,522
My line has ended!

1132
02:00:39,024 --> 02:00:41,016
My lord!

1133
02:00:54,537 --> 02:00:56,363
Rohan...

1134
02:00:57,121 --> 02:00:59,527
has deserted us.

1135
02:01:13,966 --> 02:01:17,169
Theoden's betrayed me.

1136
02:01:28,312 --> 02:01:30,138
Abandon your posts!

1137
02:01:31,189 --> 02:01:35,103
Flee! Flee for your lives!

1138
02:01:45,241 --> 02:01:46,783
Prepare for battle!

1139
02:01:47,326 --> 02:01:50,492
Hurry, men! To the wall! Defend the wall!

1140
02:01:51,663 --> 02:01:53,620
Over here!

1141
02:01:54,374 --> 02:01:56,746
Return to your posts!

1142
02:02:07,550 --> 02:02:10,171
Send these foul beasts into the abyss.

1143
02:02:20,352 --> 02:02:21,811
Stay where you are.

1144
02:02:38,783 --> 02:02:40,193
We need more rubble!

1145
02:02:40,367 --> 02:02:42,241
Watch out!

1146
02:02:42,411 --> 02:02:44,948
Down to the lower levels. Quick!

1147
02:02:46,830 --> 02:02:48,372
Double up, men!

1148
02:03:57,344 --> 02:04:00,344
Hold them back! Do not give in to fear.

1149
02:04:00,847 --> 02:04:04,345
Stand to your posts! Fight!

1150
02:04:45,005 --> 02:04:46,629
Not at the towers!

1151
02:04:46,798 --> 02:04:49,799
Aim for the trolls! Kill the trolls!

1152
02:04:50,552 --> 02:04:52,379
Bring them down!

1153
02:05:27,496 --> 02:05:29,536
Fight them back!

1154
02:05:29,707 --> 02:05:31,700
Peregrin Took!

1155
02:05:32,584 --> 02:05:35,750
- Go back to the Citadel!
- They'd called us out to fight.

1156
02:05:51,433 --> 02:05:53,805
This is no place for a Hobbit.

1157
02:06:19,537 --> 02:06:20,996
Guard of the Citadel, indeed.

1158
02:06:21,623 --> 02:06:24,955
Now, back, up the hill. Quickly. Quick!

1159
02:06:36,300 --> 02:06:39,254
What are you doing, you useless scum?!

1160
02:06:39,428 --> 02:06:41,385
The door won't give. It's too strong.

1161
02:06:47,726 --> 02:06:50,133
Get back there and smash it down.

1162
02:06:50,311 --> 02:06:52,303
But nothing can breach it.

1163
02:06:55,231 --> 02:06:57,473
Grond will breach it.

1164
02:07:00,902 --> 02:07:02,978
Bring up the wolf's head.

1165
02:07:06,157 --> 02:07:11,494
Grond! Grond! Grond! Grond!

1166
02:07:11,828 --> 02:07:15,659
Grond! Grond! Grond!

1167
02:07:17,582 --> 02:07:20,998
Grond! Grond! Grond!

1168
02:07:21,711 --> 02:07:25,374
Grond! Grond! Grond!

1169
02:07:25,796 --> 02:07:29,960
Grond! Grond! Grond!

1170
02:07:30,134 --> 02:07:33,834
Grond! Grond! Grond!!

